          "answer": "**Call your local emergency number now. Your baby needs immediate emergency care.**\n\nThe urgency tool returned \"routine\" because it did not match this description to its list. That result is wrong for these symptoms, so I am not reporting it. The emergency guidance in *Severe difficulty breathing* (educational summary, red-flag category) matches your description directly. It lists these as signs to call emergency services immediately:\n\n- **In a child:** fast breathing, and the skin sucking in between or under the ribs. You have described both.\n- **Drowsiness or exhaustion in someone struggling to breathe.** Going quiet and floppy fits this.\n\nDo not wait to see whether she improves. If you can, have someone else call while you stay with her. If her lips, face or fingertips turn blue or grey, or she becomes harder to wake, say so to the call handler straight away.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
